 * must answer it. Every refusal case implements {@link Refusal} — the transaction boundary rolls
 * back on it as on a thrown failure — and the success case never does.
 *
 * <p>Each case carries values, never identities: ids, figures, value objects and read models — no
 * aggregate root or entity, also not inside a {@code List} or {@code Optional}. A refusal case
 * carries what the refusal compared, never display text; the adapter writes the words.
 */
